# The toolchain the Aether port is built and tested against. Pins are what
# was last verified, not "latest"; bump one in the commit that needs it (or
# that re-verified the port against it), as the other Aether repos do.
#
# Install both in one step (aeb's get.sh, pinned):
#   curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aether-lang-dev/aeb/main/get.sh \
#     | AE_PIN=$AE_PIN AEB_REF=$AEB_REF sh
#
# 0.909.0 (2026-11-12): the first pin. contrib.quickjs (quickjs-ng 0.17.0)
# is the engine; std.worker's run_detached gives a tool call its thread,
# std.sync its completion flag, std.os's spawn_proc_to a bash process group.
# Verified: aeb .tests.ae (20 suites, 156 tests, workspace.sh, check_layers.sh)
# on macOS arm64, ae-x64 (Ubuntu 22.04, kernel 5.15: no Landlock ABI 2, bash
# runs unsandboxed there as upstream) and cachyos (kernel 7.3: Landlock holds).
AE_PIN=0.909.0

# v0.344 (2026-11-12): aether.program and aether.program_test with lib().
AEB_REF=v0.344
